## What happens next

Five steps take your car from your driveway to its first rental.

:::flow
Tell us about the car | We confirm fees and set your terms
Sign the agreements | Online, one for all your cars
One registry visit | We fill in the forms and come with you
Tracker and insurance | We install it and add the car
Photos and listing | Live within 1 business day
:::

1. Right after you apply, Home shows **Read your agreements**: both agreements, filled in from your application, marked "Terms pending approval". The fees and the Revenue Share read Pending approval until we set them, and the Sign button stays off.
2. When your terms are ready, Home shows **Check and sign**. Everything is filled in from your application: check the short list of key values (each has a **Fix** link) and open any document to read it in full.
3. Sign in a few steps: say you read the documents, initial the three confirmations, tick the two consents and draw your signature. Then press **Sign all**. A code to your phone or email is optional (**Verify by code**); it is asked first only if CarmaCars turns it on. One signature covers every document, in about two minutes.
4. Pay the upfront invoice: the first and last month''s insurance fee for each car (see chapter 4).
5. Upload what each car''s checklist asks for: the ownership permit, the lender''s permission if it is financed or leased, and insurance.
6. Sign Forms C and D (filled in for you) with witnesses: Form C on screen with your witness beside you, or on paper; Form D on paper, with a photo of each page from your phone (see chapter 5).

## If we need a little more

Sometimes we need one more document before we can approve your application, for example the ownership permit or the insurance slip.

1. You get an email, and Home shows "We need a little more" with the list and any note from our team.
2. Upload what is asked, or write Your answer, and press **Send my answer**.
3. We review it within 1 business day. Once we approve your application, you get an email and Home shows Check and sign.

No typing the VIN: press **Scan the barcode** and point your phone at the barcode in the driver''s door frame or at the bottom of the windshield, or **Photo of the VIN** and take a photo of it. Check the VIN shown before you continue.

**Photos:** on your car''s page, **Add photos** takes up to 30 at once, in any order. We sort them, put the outside photos on our studio background and keep the inside ones as taken. At least 10 are needed.

## A fleet supplier: lease your cars to CarmaCars

For a corporation that leases its cars to CarmaCars for a fixed amount a month. You pay CarmaCars no fees: no invoices, no debits.

1. Go to `carmacars.ca/list-your-car` and press **A corporation with a fleet? Lease your cars to us as a fleet supplier** (or choose **A corporation** in the application, then **Fleet supplier: lease your cars to CarmaCars**).
2. About you: the corporation''s legal name and number, its registered address, and the signing officer''s name and title.
3. For each car: type the VIN (the year, make and model fill in), then the plate, and mark the car **Regular** or **Troubled** (it needs work). Each tier shows its lease a month. The tier is set when you add the car and does not change.
4. Say who the car is registered to now: **My corporation**, **Me or another officer, personally** (it moves into your corporation), or **A seller: the corporation is buying it**. For the last two, enter the name and address on the ownership and the transfer or sale date.
5. Press **Continue**, check the review and press **Submit application**. The ServiceOntario forms each car needs are filled in for you at once, under **Documents**: the lease to CarmaCars (CarmaCars holds the plates while it leases the car) and, for a car not yet registered to your corporation, the transfer into it. A seller signs the transfer on the back of the ownership. Only the empty boxes are filled; you sign them in ink at ServiceOntario.
6. In your owner portal, open **Cars**, then each car, and upload its ownership (registration) copy.
7. We check each car. Once we approve it, it is on the lease at its tier and Home shows **Check and sign**: you sign the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement, the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement and Form B (the lease summary) in the owner portal, on screen (there is no paper option).

> Good to know: Home and **Money** show **Your fleet lease**: each car, its tier, its lease a month and the next payment date. The lease is paid on the 10th for the month before, with your statement; the first payment comes at least one full month after the car goes on the lease, and part months are paid by the day. Add more cars from your owner portal the same way.',
